      "content": "this is a good start and definitely covers the main points. i think it's accurate. \n\nthe thing is, looking at the draft, i'm a bit worried the term density might come up a little short for the supervisor's automated filter. they can be pretty picky about how \"technical\" the report feels. \n\ncould you flesh this out into a more detailed, multi-paragraph deep dive? try to really lean into the biochemical and molecular mechanisms involved (like the specific lipid interactions or the endosomal pathway stuff) to make sure the term density is high enough to pass. just please make sure it stays coherent and actually explains the science—dont just throw words together, but definitely make it more \"dense\" than the first version.",
