      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This research elucidates a sophisticated ionizable lipid nanoparticle (LNP) architecture engineered through precise modulation of the lipid pKa transition and hydrophobic tail branching within the endosomal acid-labile environment. By optimizing cationic-lipid-protein interactions at physiological pH, the formulation facilitates rapid endosomal escape via the proton sponge effect, thereby preventing premature lysosomal degradation of the mRNA cargo before it reaches the cytoplasm. The resulting complexes exhibit markedly enhanced transfection efficiency in non-polarized hepatic and pulmonary parenchymal cells, triggering efficient Cas9-nCas9 heterodimer assembly and specific DNA-induced double-strand breaks. Crucially, these recapitulated molecular mechanisms minimize off-target cytotoxicity and non-specific systemic inflammation, establishing a robust platform for precise CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing in clinical-grade formulations.",
      "source": "target",
