    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This investigation delineates a next-generation ionizable lipid nanoparticle (LNP) platform engineered through precise tuning of the critical pH-dependent pKa transition and hydrophobic tail branching geometries to overcome the molecular barrier of the endosomal membrane. By leveraging electrostatic lipoplex interactions, the optimized formulation induces rapid endosomal rupture via the proton sponge mechanism, ensuring efficient mRNA cytosolic delivery and subsequent formation of high-fidelity RNP complexes where Cas9 প্রদর্শক subunits assume their catalytically active conformation. These advanced systems demonstrate superior transduction kinetics within hepatocytes and pneumocytes by bypassing early endosomal acidification, thereby facilitating robust CRISPR-Cas9 mediated genome editing with minimal off-target effects and suppressed cytokine storm cascades. Consequently, the strategic manipulation of lipid phase behavior and intracellular trafficking pathways establishes a clinically viable architecture for high-throughput nucleic acid therapeutics requiring sub-nanometer precision in genomic correction.",
      "source": "target",
